-- title:
--   A multiple HNN extension of a finitely presented group along finite subgroups, with finitely many stable letters, is finitely presented
-- statement:
--   Let $H$ be a finitely presented group (`H : Type*` with `[Group H]` and `[Group.IsFinitelyPresented H]`) and let `I : Type*` be a finite index type (`[Finite I]`). For each $i \in I$ let $A_i, B_i \le H$ be subgroups (`A B : I → Subgroup H`) with $A_i$ finite (`[∀ i, Finite (A i)]`), and let $\varphi_i : A_i \to B_i$ be a group isomorphism (`φ : ∀ i, A i ≃* B i`). Then the multiple HNN extension
--   $$\mathrm{HNN}(H; A_i \xrightarrow{\varphi_i} B_i) \;=\; \bigl\langle\, H,\ t_i\ (i \in I) \;\bigm|\; t_i\, a\, t_i^{-1} = \varphi_i(a) \ \ (i \in I,\ a \in A_i) \,\bigr\rangle$$
--   is finitely presented (`Group.IsFinitelyPresented (MultipleHNN.Extension A B φ)`, Mathlib's notion).
--
--   Here `MultipleHNN.Extension A B φ` is the free product of $H$ with the free group on $I$ (`Monoid.Coprod H (FreeGroup I)`) divided by the congruence generated by the relations $t_i\,a = \varphi_i(a)\,t_i$ for $i \in I$ and $a \in A_i$, with its quotient group structure. The extension adds finitely many generators $t_i$ and, because every $A_i$ is finite, finitely many relations to a finite presentation of $H$.
--
--   Lean: `OAI.KaplanskyCounterexample.CurrentMain.multipleHNN_finitelyPresented`, OpenAI's lemma of that name in `lean/OAI/RingTheory/DirectFiniteness/HNNPresentation.lean`. `Extension` and its group structure come from the definitions bundle `OAIQWKAPHNN`, which contains only OpenAI's multiple-HNN construction and imports nothing but Mathlib.
-- source:
--   G. Higman, B. H. Neumann and H. Neumann, Embedding theorems for groups, J. London Math. Soc. 24 (1949), 247–254 (the HNN construction). Lean proof: OpenAI, A Counterexample to Kaplansky's Direct-Finiteness Conjecture in Characteristic Two, OpenAI Math Release, September 23, 2026, https://github.com/openai/math (result family 197; paper: https://github.com/openai/math/blob/adc7f1241b42e322a6451854ab7e4b4c146bf78a/preprints/A-Counterexample-to-Kaplanskys-Direct-Finiteness-Conjecture-in-Characteristic-Two-September-23-2026/paper.pdf; Apache License 2.0); Lean: https://github.com/openai/math/blob/adc7f1241b42e322a6451854ab7e4b4c146bf78a/lean/OAI/RingTheory/DirectFiniteness/HNNPresentation.lean (declaration OAI.KaplanskyCounterexample.CurrentMain.multipleHNN_finitelyPresented)

